diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 23d8ff4..0d380f8 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 - **CPAC real telemetry ingestion (§5 record scoring + Command Code extraction)**: the CPAC utility is no longer simulated-only. New `scripts/extract-commandcode-telemetry.sh`/`.ps1` convert a Command Code session transcript (`~/.commandcode/projects/<slug>/<session>.jsonl`, JSONL schema v3) into the standardized telemetry record defined in `docs/BENCHMARK-METHODOLOGY.md` §5 — successful-turn token sums split from rework turns by a documented turn-walk rule, tool-call totals with a best-effort search/edit/verify classification, human interventions (user prompts after the first), wall clock from the first/last event timestamps, the last assistant model, and cache-read tokens reported but excluded from `C_inference` (the v1 cache convention, since §2 prices a single input tier); `accepted` defaults to `false` with a loud stderr note because acceptance is a human judgment. `scripts/measure-cpac.sh`/`.ps1` now score such a record from a path argument: required keys validated fail-closed (exit `2` with `CPAC|ERROR|MISSING_KEY|<key>` / `BAD_VALUE` / `UNREADABLE` diagnostics) and a measured scorecard plus a `CPAC|MEASURED|...` machine line printed, with new pricing override flags (`--price-in/--price-out/--rework-tool-cost/--human-rate`; PS `-PriceIn/-PriceOut/-ReworkToolCost/-HumanRate`) for cross-model repricing. Both twins reach byte-identical records and machine lines from identical inputs (verified on a real transcript); the Bash extractor is a dependency-free awk state machine (no jq/python/node), and transcript-derived values never re-enter the shell parser. Rework-loop failure detection is a documented heuristic (Command Code schema v3 records no tool exit codes), approximating dimension 3's non-zero-exit-code measurement via a pattern list over tool-result text (`--error-patterns` overridable). A fixture harness (`scripts/tests/run-cpac-ingestion-tests.sh`/`.ps1`, 17 Bash / 16 PowerShell paired cases) pins the formula expectations, machine lines, fail-closed diagnostics (including tail-anchored values and negative-metric rejection added by the post-audit hardening), an stderr-empty-on-valid-run regression, exact extraction fields, and an extraction→scoring end-to-end case; `measure-cpac.sh`/`.ps1` (previously syntax-checked nowhere) and the new scripts join both CI syntax lists and both run legs, with matching `CONTRIBUTING.md` validation-command entries. The simulated scorecard is preserved, labeled, behind `--demo`/`-Demo`. Behavior-surface paths: `scripts/measure-cpac.sh`, `scripts/measure-cpac.ps1`, `scripts/extract-commandcode-telemetry.sh`, `scripts/extract-commandcode-telemetry.ps1`, `scripts/tests/run-cpac-ingestion-tests.sh`, `scripts/tests/run-cpac-ingestion-tests.ps1`, `scripts/tests/fixtures/cpac-ingestion/`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `docs/BENCHMARK-METHODOLOGY.md`, `docs/BENCHMARKS.md`, `docs/specs/SPEC-empirical-benchmark.md`, `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/tasks/TASK-2026-10-25-cpac-telemetry-ingestion.md`.
 
 ### Changed
+- **Context-economy transitive discovery route now carries a static regression guard (issue #596)**: `protocols/context-economy.md` §11's Discovery route paragraph no longer claims that no automated check exercises the path to that file; it now records that both behavioral-contract suites assert the transitive route — the Balanced and Lite directive templates name `setup` in their protocols line, `protocols/setup.md`'s *Workflows & Protocols Reference* lists `context-economy.md`, and `docs/WORKFLOW-MAP.md` links it — while stating plainly that discovery has not been validated with recorded live transcripts and that Balanced/Lite discoverability and sufficiency remain open acceptance evidence. The new `AT` scenario in `scripts/tests/run-behavioral-contract-tests.sh` and its `.ps1` twin pins those four links, rejects the retired "no automated check exercises it" claim, and keeps the live-transcript gap asserted. Documentation and test-only: the directive templates, `protocols/setup.md`, `docs/WORKFLOW-MAP.md`, and the advisory enforcement boundary are unchanged.
 - **CPAC CLI default output and §2B rework-formula alignment**: a bare `measure-cpac.sh`/`.ps1` invocation now prints usage instead of defaulting to the simulated scorecard (the simulation moves behind `--demo`/`-Demo`, still labeled), so an unlabeled simulated table can no longer appear to be a measurement; `calculate_cpac` now implements the documented §2B rework formula — `C_rework = Σ(T_loop × P_avg + τ_tool)`, i.e. rework-loop tokens priced at the same in/out rates plus the per-loop tool execution cost, excluded from `C_inference` — replacing the previous flat per-loop penalty, with the self-test expectations recomputed (Test 2 now prices 12,000/2,100 loop tokens across 3 loops: `8.7725`) and the machine-line money fields of both twins formatted invariantly to 4 decimals so twin outputs match regardless of runner locale. The PowerShell twin reads the record's string fields (`scenario_id`, `condition`, `model`, `timestamp`) textually rather than from the parsed object, because `ConvertFrom-Json` silently converts ISO-8601 values to `[datetime]`. Behavior-surface paths: `scripts/measure-cpac.sh`, `scripts/measure-cpac.ps1`, `docs/BENCHMARK-METHODOLOGY.md`.
 
 ### Fixed
